-- title:
--   Chart functions with mathfrak m_A-integral q-expansion vanish at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of order $q\ell$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ for the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell)\,M'$ (the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}=q^{-1}+\dots$, assumed nonzero, and write $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A\,K\,j$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with $X=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A\,K\,j$ the pushout of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ and $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the corresponding $j^{-1}$-chart along their common middle scheme. Let $z$ be a point of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section of $X$ obtained from $\varpi$ along $X\to\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$, and let $y\in\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ be a point mapping to $z$ under the canonical map $\mathrm{Spec}\,C\to X$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C\to\Omega$ with kernel the prime ideal $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Then every $a\in C$ all of whose Laurent coefficients (in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$) lie in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$ belongs to the prime ideal $y$.
--
--   This is the statement that the supersingular closed point $y$ of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model lies on the component through the cusp $\infty$: the "Gauss set" of chart functions whose $q$-expansion coefficients are all in $\mathfrak m_A$ is contained in $y$. It is the input of the comparison [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_mem_comap_drinfeldChart_iff_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.forall_mem_comap_drinfeldChart_iff_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_linearPart_riders_twoChartIntegralModel), which identifies the functions vanishing at $y$ with those having $q$-expansion reducing to zero.
